> 1.  When the robot is a mobile platform, the "platform\-oriented" development mode may require a person to follow the vehicle, which is obviously inefficient and poses certain safety hazards;
>     
> 2.  The "platform\-oriented" development mode is also constrained by many factors such as the environment and terrain;
>     
> 3.  There may be a one\-to\-many relationship between the robot and developers, that is, multiple development or test engineers use the same device, and under the "platform\-oriented" development mode, resource contention will inevitably occur;
>
